<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Big Three banks rise on privatisation hope.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Big Three banks rise on privatisation hope.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Big Three state-run banks rose in mid-morning trade on Friday on expectations that the government will soon privatise the banks, brokers said.</p>
<p>A government panel has suggested the Provincial Assembly abolish its 1989 decision not to let state stakes in the Big Three state-run banks fall below 51 percent, officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>With 60 minutes left, Chang Hwa Bank was up T$2 or 1.08 percent to T$188, First Bank rose T$2 or 1.06 percent to T$190 and Hua Nan Bank rose T$1 or 0.69 percent to T$146.5.</p>
</text>
